EDT Automation Project - Complete End-to-End Overview
Project Name

EDT Automation using Python and Large Language Models (Claude AI)

Project Summary

EDT Automation was an AI-powered document processing and workflow automation system developed to reduce manual effort in extracting, validating, analyzing, and transforming enterprise documents. The solution leveraged Python-based automation, Large Language Models (LLMs), and Claude AI to intelligently process unstructured data and generate structured outputs with minimal human intervention.

The primary objective was to automate repetitive document-related tasks, improve data accuracy, reduce turnaround time, and increase operational efficiency.

Business Problem

Before automation:

Large volumes of documents were processed manually.
Employees spent significant time extracting required information.
Human errors occurred during data entry.
Processing turnaround time was high.
Handling multiple document formats was difficult.
Goal

Build an intelligent automation system that can:

Read documents automatically.
Understand document content using LLMs.
Extract relevant information.
Validate extracted data.
Generate structured outputs.
Automate downstream workflows.
